  "security_implications": "Under hmac_en_i=1 and pad selection (SelIPad/SelOPad), sha_rdata_o drives key-dependent pad data with mask = '1 (all ones). If the downstream SHA engine expects masked data for side-channel protection, this unconditionally clear mask may bypass that protection, leading to leakage of the HMAC key through power/EM side channels. The default fallback also implies that any illegal sel_rdata selects fifo_rdata_i, which could expose internal state or hide a silent failure.",
